          small network  -  secure by default  -  no nonsense
                  powered by SekurIRCd v0.8.4

=====================================================================
 [ NETWORK ]
=====================================================================

  Plaintext ........ port 6667
  TLS/SSL .......... port 6697   (recommended - gets you user mode +z)
  Hostnames ........ cloaked; your real IP is not shown to other users
  Services ......... ChanServ   /msg ChanServ HELP
  Accounts ......... SASL PLAIN, or /REGISTER <account> <password>

=====================================================================
 [ CHANNELS ]
=====================================================================

  #SekurNet ........ main lobby - say hi
  #help ............ questions about the network or your client
  #SekurIRCd-dev ... ircd development, live commit/PR feed

  Want your own channel? See [ REGISTERING A CHANNEL ] below.

=====================================================================
 [ RULES ]
=====================================================================

  By connecting you agree to the following. No exceptions.

   1. Be civil. No harassment, hate speech, threats or doxxing.
   2. No flooding, spamming, advertising or mass-highlighting.
   3. No botnets, drones, clones or connection proxies for abuse.
      Bots are fine if they behave and a channel op allows them.
   4. No warez, cracks, malware, stolen data or illegal content.
   5. No porn or NSFW content outside channels set up for it.
   6. No nick or channel squatting, and no impersonating staff.
   7. Channel ops run their channels; network staff run the network.
      Take disputes to #help, not to the channel you got kicked from.
   8. Don't ask for oper. If we need you, we'll ask you.

  Breaking the rules gets you a kick, a K-line or a permanent ban -
  our call, no appeals via PM spam. Incidents may be reported to
  your provider. If you wouldn't let your kids do it at home, don't
  do it here.

=====================================================================
 [ REGISTERING A CHANNEL ]
=====================================================================

  1. Create it and hold op:   /JOIN #mychannel
  2. Register it:             /msg ChanServ REGISTER #mychannel <pass>
  3. Keep it alive (optional) /msg ChanServ JOIN #mychannel <pass>
     ChanServ stays inside, so the channel survives everyone leaving.

  Lost op after a reconnect? Get it back with:

     /msg ChanServ IDENTIFY #mychannel <pass>

  Share ops without sharing the password:
     /msg ChanServ ACCESS #mychannel ADD *!*@their.host o <pass>

  Pick a strong channel password and keep it to yourself.
  Full command list: /msg ChanServ HELP

=====================================================================
 [ PRIVACY ]
=====================================================================

  Server logs are kept for abuse handling only and are never sold
  or shared. Staff never ask for your password - don't give it out.

=====================================================================

  Type /MOTD to read this again.        Be smart. Be chill. Have fun.

